# ============================================================
# Alwazir — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you need:
#     cp .env.example .env
# (The real .env is gitignored — never commit it. It contains
# your database password.)
#
# On Vercel you do NOT need a .env file — set these same
# variables in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables instead.
# ============================================================

# ---------- Database (pick ONE) ----------

# Option A — Neon Postgres (recommended)
# A PostgreSQL connection string from the Neon console.
# When set, EVERYTHING (settings, products, images) is stored in
# Postgres — tables are created automatically and a fresh database
# is seeded with the default store. This is all you need to add:
#
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxxx-xxxxx-pooler.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/alwazir?sslmode=require
#
# How to get it:
#   1. Sign in at https://neon.tech → New Project
#      (pick any region, e.g. us-east-2)
#   2. Dashboard → "Connection details" → copy the CONNECTION
#      STRING (the "pooled" endpoint is the one to use)
#   3. Paste it as DATABASE_URL below
#
# DATABASE_URL=

# Option B — Vercel Blob (alternative; used when DATABASE_URL is
# empty). Token from Vercel → project → Storage → your Blob store.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# If neither is set, the app stores data in a local data/db.json
# file + public/uploads/ (only useful for npm start on one machine).
